{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNpHKdZtCodVtPHxyxC2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a timeline card whose rows overflow its 540 height: 86+70+32+56+70+56+32+56+56 = 514, plus the 67 start offset gives 581, which spills past 540. Growing the card to 600 runs into the bottom cards at y=628. I instead compress the rows to 74,62,28,48,58,48,28,48,48 = 442, so 67+442 = 509, safely under 540.\n\nThe Complete Task chart's line stops short of its last dot because Figma shifts vector geometry so the bbox starts at the origin, so I set pv.x and pv.y from the computed mins, matching the helper that worked on the dashboard. Dots sit at 140,232,324,415,507,598,690, roughly 91.5 = 572/6 apart.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":105309,"input_tokens":1,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":105309}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b035988-a95d-4967-90e1-871b84812e81","uuid":"42ed03e5-1cb7-4c44-af16-25473fdf0533","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:10:46.426Z","thinking_duration_ms":14546}
