{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNpdm8vOZKYuKKWkVcWy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a card content overflow: on cover cards the avatar row sits at 215 versus a card height of 146, spilling from y 166..312 past the card bottom at 202. With top=60 and cover, my=top+74=134, and 134+21=155 exceeds 146. One fix is my=CH-28=118, avatars 21 high at 118..139, but the date icon at top+52=112 and its text at 110 collide with 118, and a taller card of 158 breaks the column: 56+3*158=530 exceeds 506, and 3*152=512 also overflows.\n\nI settle on explicit offsets. Cover: cover y10..50, tag y=56 (18 high), title y=78, date y=100..112, meta y=120..141, all inside 146. No-cover: tag y=12, title y=34, date y=56..68, meta y=120 bottom-aligned. No separators. This also fixes the \"Onboarding copy\" card in the In Progress column, where top=60 gave my=134 and overflowed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":134889,"input_tokens":1,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":134889}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b035988-a95d-4967-90e1-871b84812e81","uuid":"a36f6d09-4d5b-4ba4-b04e-4ed6034f570a","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:15:19.079Z","thinking_duration_ms":12680}
